## Python micro‑service strictness
> Mirrors the spirit of the TS rules; keeps the micro‑service safe, typed, and deterministic.

| Category | Rule |
|----------|------|
| **.venv** | All commands (pip, python, pytest) must be run from within the activated project .venv | 
| **Interpreter** | Target **Python 3.9.6** |
| **Testing** | Use **pytest**; all new modules need matching `tests/` |
| **Static typing** | Mandatory `mypy --strict` during CI; no `Any` leaks |
| **Code formatting** | Enforce **black** (`line-length = 100`) + **isort** |
| **Linting** | ruff --select all |
| **Imports** | Absolute imports inside package; no implicit relative (`from .foo import *`) |
| **Type hints** | Full type hints on **all** public / exported functions & class methods |
| **Docstrings** | Google‑style: `Args`, `Returns`, `Raises`, `Example`; top‑level module docstring required |
| **Exceptions** | Raise custom subclasses of `Exception`; never bare `ValueError` unless obvious |
| **Data models** | Use `pydantic.BaseModel` (or `dataclasses.dataclass` with type hints) for structured payloads |
| **Logging** | Use `logging` std‑lib — never `print()` except in CLIs |
| **Mutability traps** | No mutable default args (`def fn(x: list = [])` ❌) |
| **I/O** | Wrap external I/O (HTTP, DB) in retry‑aware helpers; surface `TimeoutError` or `HTTPError` |
| **Performance** | Prefer asyncio tasks for network concurrency; forbid `time.sleep()` in async fns |
| **Security** | No plaintext secrets; expect `os.environ`‑injected config |

